==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[lede#Etymology_1|lede]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|leod||people|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term/t|ang|lēode}} {{gloss|"people, men"; plural of {{term/t|ang|lēod||person, man}}}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*liudiz|*liudīz|people}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*(e)lewədh-||man, people}}. Cognate with {{etyl|sco|-}} {{term|lede||people|lang=sco}}, {{etyl|fy|-}} {{term|lie||people|lang=fy}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|lieden||people|lang=nl}} and {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|lui|lui(den)|people|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Leute||people|lang=de}}, {{etyl|no|-}} {{term|lyd||people|lang=no}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|lēd|lē-ōd}}, {{IPA|/liːd/|/liːod/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/li:d/|/li:od/}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|lead}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|leod|pl2=leods}}

# {{form of|Alternative or obsolete form|lede|lang=en}}.
# {{context|collectively|obsolete|lang=en}} [[people|People]].
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} A [[people]], [[nation]], people group.
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} A [[man]], [[person]].

===Anagrams===
* [[dole#English|dole]], [[lode#English|lode]], [[olde#English|olde]], [[OLED#English|OLED]]

